ensory-motor pattern", "Thoracic outlet syndrome: considered but outcompeted by apical alarm features", "Steroid-induced myopathy: unlikely to explain sensory loss and pain profile"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional weight loss", "Longstanding tobacco use (2-pack/day since age 25)", "Hypertension with elevated temperature (37.5°C)", "Steroid use with diabetes (risk for metabolic complications)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Neoplastic Processes in the Thorax (Apical/Brachial Plexus Involvement)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.7590361445783134, "posterior": 0.3777317474085172, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Positional independence of symptoms strongly contradicts vascular compression mechanisms in bodybuilders."], "evidence_against": ["Non-positional symptoms and metabolic risks mildly support neurological causes but lack specificity."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Neurological Disorders with Subacute Onset", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.12048192771084336, "posterior": 0.1243001934892974, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Subacute progression and constitutional symptoms align with paraneoplastic/progressive neurological causes, but lack specificity for definitive classification."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of tumor evidence and presence of steroid neuropathy risk moderately reduce neurological disorder probability."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification